# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VRMPet
#
# Source that IS tracked: CMakeLists.txt, build.sh, REPORT.md, docs/, src/,
# tools/, assets/, and third_party/wicked_importer/.
#
#   * docs/ holds the rendered comparisons REPORT.md embeds. Those images are
#     tracked - a clone without them shows five broken images - but the one
#     working document that lives there is not. See the last section.
#   * third_party/wicked_importer/ is a deliberate byte-for-byte copy of the
#     engine's Editor/ModelImporter_GLTF.cpp - see REPORT.md section 4.4 - so it
#     must stay in the repository. .gitattributes keeps line endings away from
#     it so the copy really is byte-for-byte on every machine.
#   * assets/ holds the avatar and its idle loop. These are INPUTS, not build
#     output: they are what the tool is a tool for. The copies CMake stages into
#     build/run/assets/ are derived, and build/ is ignored wholesale.
#
# Everything else below is generated.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build tree
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build.sh configures into build/ and copies VRMPet.exe, dxcompiler.dll, the
# compiled shaders and assets/ into build/run/. All of it is derived:
# CMakeCache.txt, the Ninja files, object files, and every capture the tool
# produces.
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/

# build.sh writes its full transcript here.
build_vrmpet.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CMake
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeUserPresets.json
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
install_manifest.txt
compile_commands.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MSVC / Windows toolchain
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.obj
*.o
*.exe
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.idb
*.res
*.tlog
*.lastbuildstate
*.log

# Generated Visual Studio project files, for anyone who configures with -G VS.
.vs/
*.sln
*.vcxproj
*.vcxproj.filters
*.vcxproj.user

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Capture output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VRMPet.exe writes these into its output directory, and the tools in tools/
# write the derived images next to them. This is belt and braces: the tool is
# normally run from build/run, which is ignored wholesale above. The names are
# listed individually rather than with a blanket *.png so a screenshot that is
# worth keeping can still be committed - the side-by-side comparisons in
# REPORT.md are exactly that, and they live in docs/ instead.
mask_default.png
mask_user.png
mask_nostencil.png
background.png
color.png
engine.log
log.txt
run.log
diff_full.png
diff_head.png
mask_default_head.png
mask_user_head.png
mask_default_over_checker.png
mask_user_over_checker.png
head_composite_vs_truth.png

# Desktop grabs and the comparisons built from them, for anyone who runs the
# tool from the project root rather than from build/run.
#
# A desktop grab is a picture of whatever else was on screen. It is never worth
# committing - see the note in tools/grab_desktop.ps1 - so it is ignored by
# shape as well as by the specific names the verification runs used. docs/ is
# NOT covered: what lives there is rendered engine output only.
desktop*.png
grab*.png
*_grab.png
*_desktop.png
anim_*.png
final_*.png
*_compare.png
overlay_motion.png
head_compare.png

# Scratch directories the verification runs write into.
animoff/
animon/
front_off/
front_on/
headoff/
headon/
headoff2/
headon2/
lookat_on/
lk/
m_off/
m_on/
m_onlk/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working documents
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A design document is a working document: a plan, written to be revised or
# thrown away, not an artifact of the tool. It is kept on disk so it can be
# read and edited, and deliberately kept out of the repository so a plan that
# changes its mind does not leave a trail in the history. REPORT.md is the
# opposite - it records what was measured and is meant to be committed.
#
# The path is given in full rather than as `docs/*.md` on purpose: if a second
# design document is ever worth committing, this line should be reconsidered
# deliberately rather than silently catching it.
#
# NOTE: docs/ itself is NOT ignored. The five PNGs there are rendered engine
# output and REPORT.md embeds them by name. Ignoring the directory would break
# every one of those images in a fresh clone - which is exactly the mistake
# this note exists to prevent.
docs/DESIGN-voice-and-chat.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.env
